  "notes": "Atlanta's strip-club-facing bench: bright leads over hard claps and a bounce-forward kick. Three things separate it from the minimal-melodic bench next to it — the clap is layered two or three deep (`snare.layered` with a wide `layerClapOffsetMs` [2,7] for the stacked one-shots the research says became a widely-circulated sound), the rolls come under hooks rather than everywhere (`hihat.fill.prob` 0.6), and it is the only entry on this bench whose scale pool carries real `major` weight, because the research names occasional major-mode club cuts. Melody is bell/marimba/pluck over a 2-bar loop with a wide register split, so the lead sits at 74–98 over an 808 at 17–32 and the middle stays empty. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it medium and found no substantial workflow interview. The inferred parameters are the kick grammar — `kick.densityPerBar`, `syncopation` and `tresilloBias` are read off \"kick with 16th pickups\" and the research marks that claim [LOW-CONF] — and the roll frequency. ⚠ `chords.impliedByRiff` is set and the two families are exactly what the research names, \"static i vamps and i–VI\"; the chord part's variety comes from `chordDurationBeats` and the three harmonic rhythms rather than from progressions this producer does not play.",
